   <narrative xml:lang="EN">London School of Economics and Political Science</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Jobs Dataset: G2LM|LIC Data Building Component</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Although researchers in development economics have made great progress in understanding the link between gender, jobs and poverty by rigorous evaluation of policies at a very micro level, aggregating this knowledge and assessing its external validity is still lagging behind. The data building activities within the G2LM-LIC project will address this challenge and facilitate the next stage of research on jobs and poverty by building the Global Jobs Database (GJD) which acts as a platform to harmonise all available micro datasets that contain information on labour market activities and poverty to create a multi-country macro data-set that contains, at a minimum: labor force participation, occupational choice (sector, casual vs regular, wage vs self-employment), earnings, hours worked, seasonality all by gender, ethnicity (where relevant), education, and wealth.</narrative>
  </description>
